# Copy to .env (optional). .env is gitignored.
#
# omi-local: this app talks only to YOUR server. The server address, username and
# password are entered on the sign-in screen (or Settings → Account → Server) and
# kept in the app's user data — nothing about the server is baked into the build.
# No Firebase project, no Omi cloud, no analytics or crash-report keys.
#
# Runtime environment variables (not build-time; set them when launching the app):
#   OMI_SERVER_URL       pin the server for this install (managed setups, tests)
#   OMI_UPDATE_FEED_URL  a self-hosted electron-builder "generic" update feed;
#                        unset (default) = the app never checks for updates

# Public share origin for conversation links. Unset = links are built on your
# server's address.
# VITE_OMI_SHARE_BASE_URL=
